Hello World!

## Firecrawl integration

This repo wires a minimal, real [Firecrawl](https://www.firecrawl.dev) scrape:
`main.py` scrapes a single page and prints its Markdown.

### Setup

1. Install dependencies:

       pip install -r requirements.txt

2. Provide your API key — copy `.env.example` to `.env` and set it, or export it:

       export FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=fc-your-api-key-here

### Run

    python main.py                  # scrapes https://example.com
    python main.py https://news.ycombinator.com

The wired call is `firecrawl.scrape(url, formats=["markdown"])` (see `main.py`),
returning a document whose `.markdown` field is printed to stdout.
